Found under k315 (2026-10-31). Keys/Secure.pm `_reroll_robocop` reads Config::robocop_enabled only AFTER the keys are switched to secure mode, and `ocp keys secure` never runs validate(). Since k315 a malformed robocop: croaks there with validate()'s line -- better than before (robocop: no read as on and rolled robocop's credentials out), but the command stops halfway, after the first PIN and the switch.

Fix: read robocop_enabled (or run validate()) before the first PIN, so a malformed ocp.yaml stops `ocp keys secure` before it changes anything.

Done = a malformed robocop: stops `ocp keys secure` before the first prompt and before any file is written (test), the message is validate()'s line on STDERR.

